# Cargo build output
/target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed for this crate and its example. Both build cdylib /
# staticlib artifacts for C++ consumers, so they are applications, not
# libraries, and need a reproducible dependency set. Leaving them unpinned made
# CI re-resolve on every run, which broke the build the moment aws-smithy-runtime
# 1.14.1 raised its aws-smithy-types requirement to ^1.7.0 while aws-config
# 1.12.0 still capped aws-smithy-json at ^0.63 — an unsatisfiable pair.

